It's **Lakefront Brewery**, in the Beerline B neighborhood on the north side of Milwaukee's RiverWalk. The database puts it at about 43.0547, -87.9052, which is just north of downtown. It has a beer hall, the Lakefront Brewery Beer Hall, next to the brewery.

According to [Beyond The Miles](w2), the brewery has operated since 1987. Two brothers started it with mostly used equipment, including a piece seen in the Laverne & Shirley opening credits, which they got from Schlitz. [The Royal Tour](w4) quotes co-founder Russ Klisch on how it began as a tiny 55-gallon brewery in an old bakery. His brother was a Milwaukee police officer. [No Home Just Roam](w1) describes the brewery tour, where visitors sing the Laverne & Shirley theme in the bottling room.

