The aquarium is the **Alaska SeaLife Center** at 301 Railway Avenue in Seward, on Resurrection Bay.

[Local Adventurer](w2) says it's unusual because it combines a public aquarium with a marine research center. The same page says it's the state's only permanent marine mammal rehab facility. [Wikipedia](w6) gives the same description of it as a public aquarium and Alaska's only permanent marine mammal rehabilitation facility. It opened in May 1998. Visitors can see puffins, sea lions, octopuses and salmon life stages. They can also see orphaned or injured animals being cared for, as described by [No Home Just Roam](w3).

