The airport you're thinking of is most likely **Telluride Regional Airport** in the Rocky Mountains of Colorado.

One travel writer, at [My Travelling Circus](w1), compared the Paro landing to Telluride. They said that at Telluride you land on top of a cliff in the middle of the Rockies. The airport sits on a high mesa, so the runway ends at a drop-off. It's often listed among the most dramatic airports in the US. I found the airport in the places database, but I didn't confirm the cliff-edge detail beyond that travel account.

