Truth or Consequences has several hot spring facilities, so there isn't just one answer. The best-known is **Riverbend Hot Springs**. It sits on the Rio Grande, and its soaking pools overlook the river. [New Mexico Travel Guy](w1) calls it perhaps the most iconic soak in town. [Brooke Beyond](w5) describes about a dozen rock pools behind an ivy-covered gate. Hourly passes cost about $25–30 for 1–2 people when that post was written, and prices may have changed.

Another option is **Las Palomas Hot Springs Spa**. [Colorado Traveling Ducks](w2) describes soaking in a private 103°F mineral pool there. That post calls it "La Paloma Hot Springs and Spa", which is probably the same place. The database lists it as Las Palomas, and it didn't confirm the two names are the same.

{"map": [{"ref": "W1216811075"}, {"ref": "N4505627776"}]}

