Yes, the tour stops at Casa Calvet. [Globetrotter Girls](w1) says the 2.5-hour "On the Trail of Gaudí" e-bike tour (about US$28) includes it. I only found that one source for the stop, so check the current itinerary with the tour operator before you book.

Casa Calvet is in the Eixample district, in the part called la Dreta de l'Eixample, in central Barcelona. It's at roughly 41.3908, 2.1732. [Eternal Arrival](w3) says it's a block north of Urquinaona metro, and [The Geographical Cure](w4) lists the same station (L1 and L4). Eternal Arrival also puts it about a 25-minute walk south of the Sagrada Família. It's an early Gaudí work. Today it houses a restaurant, which [The Geographical Cure](w4) says is open Monday to Saturday, 1 pm to 11 pm.

